 "units_spent": 6225,
 "question": "The inventory holds 253,988 pages and 99.97 per cent of them are about the same eleven countries the eleven searcher markets live in. For a travel-connectivity product that is backwards: the commercial moment is a person in one country about to travel to another. This asks whether the four largest markets search for places OUTSIDE their own country, and how much.",
 "method": "Four searcher markets, each asked only about places that are not in its own country. Two kinds of keyword in every block: the connectivity intent on a destination (esim <country>), and the travel-information intent on a named entity or a country-level list that matches a family the pipeline already builds (beaches, hiking, neighbourhoods, things to see). No keyword was invented from a template: each is a phrasing a speaker of that language uses.",
 "result": {
  "keywords_tested": 193,
  "keywords_with_volume": 192,
  "keywords_at_zero": [
   "zermatt escursioni"
  ],
  "strongest_entity_per_market": {
   "de-DE": "hallstatt 42,000 at KD 0, zell am see 29,000, kappadokien 27,000, plitvicer seen 18,000",
   "it-IT": "cappadocia 58,000, saranda 26,000, monte fuji 14,000, chefchaouen 13,000, pamukkale 13,000",
   "ja-JP": "カッパドキア 71,000, セブ島 65,000, タージマハル 25,000, アンコールワット 22,000",
   "en-US": "machu picchu 230,000, taj mahal 173,000, banff national park 141,000, mount fuji 85,000"
  },
  "highest_cpc_observed_cents": 300
 },
 "reading": "192 of 193 keywords carry volume, and the single zero is a bad Italian phrasing (zermatt escursioni) rather than an absent audience: esim svizzera in the same block returns 1,400. In every one of the four markets the strongest entity measured is in a country the pipeline has no pages for at all. German searchers want Hallstatt (42,000) more than almost anything measured inside Germany; Japanese searchers want Cappadocia (71,000) and Cebu (65,000); the Italian market wants Saranda in Albania (26,000), a country with zero rows today. The eSIM intent sits on the same axis and carries the commercial value: esim turkey at $2.50 CPC in en-US, esim tuerkei 13,000 in de-DE.",
 "what_this_does_NOT_license": "It does not license letting every city in a measured country inherit every market. That is the Aba, Nigeria error already recorded in markets_for(): a country having demand is not evidence that an arbitrary town inside it does. The bound this measurement supports is narrower and is stated in the plan: a place in a new destination country earns a market only when the country carries measured demand in that language AND the entity itself carries an independent mark in that language, which is a Wikipedia sitelink or an OSM name:<lang> tag. The entity-level demand above is measured; the per-entity extension of it is a labelled proxy, never presented as measured volume.",
